WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.571
- This looks like a big baguette,

00:00:02.571 --> 00:00:03.870
but it's not.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.240
It's a giant log of cookie.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.823
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:12.803
Hey, what's up?

00:00:12.803 --> 00:00:15.990
My name is Tway, and
welcome to "Making it Big",

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.270
the show where we take your favorite foods

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.130
and turn it giant,

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.270
colossal,

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.340
gargantuan.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:23.173
(high-pitched tone)

00:00:23.173 --> 00:00:24.720
I have a very special guest today,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.940
and it just happens to be her birthday,

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.700
so I really have to do a great job

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.950
at whatever she challenges me to do.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.251
So let's give it up for the birthday girl!

00:00:34.251 --> 00:00:35.394
(crew cheers)

00:00:35.394 --> 00:00:36.227
Welcome.

00:00:36.227 --> 00:00:39.330
What do I see in your hands?

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.996
- Only one of my favorite
childhood snacks.

00:00:41.996 --> 00:00:43.297
Pocky!

00:00:43.297 --> 00:00:44.130
- Interesting.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.110
These are actually the opposite of big.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.490
They're pretty small.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:48.780
- They're so small. Yeah.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.340
- How big do we want this?

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.480
- Humongous.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.770
Like a light saber.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.140
- Flavor wise, what flavors
are we working with?

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.760
- Chocolate, matcha, strawberry,

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:57.600
and cookies and cream.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.100
- Oh, these are really good flavors.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:00:59.970
- I got good taste.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:02.010
- Do you want me to pick one?

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:02.940
- All of them.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:03.773
- Oh.

00:01:03.773 --> 00:01:04.975
- You're Tway, so you can do it.

00:01:04.975 --> 00:01:05.808
(Tway laughs)

00:01:05.808 --> 00:01:06.750
I'm very excited.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.060
This will be the best birthday gift ever.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:10.680
I really appreciate you.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:11.730
Good luck.
- Thanks.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:12.641
- [Jasmine] Good luck.

00:01:12.641 --> 00:01:14.970
(Tway sighs)

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.092
- Let's do this.

00:01:16.092 --> 00:01:17.520
(jazzy music)

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.390
The fact that I have
this mountain of butter

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.700
and this mountain of flour

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.800
and it all has to be used

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.870
is a little bit daunting.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:31.860
I have to nail this
shortbread cookie dough.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:32.970
Two pounds of flour.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.310
It's gonna go right
into my food processor.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.450
About a cup of sugar,

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.980
a tablespoon of baking powder,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.560
one and a half teaspoons of kosher salt.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.020
Worried for this machine,

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.240
'cause it might overheat,

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.433
but keep a close eye on it.

00:01:48.433 --> 00:01:50.700
(processor whirs)

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.060
Okay, and then one pound
of butter right into here.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:57.753
Okay, I'm gonna give this a pulse.

00:01:57.753 --> 00:01:59.190
(processor whirs)

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:00.960
Most of the equipment here that we have

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.200
aren't really equipped to make big food.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.137
I'm gonna try my best to not break it.

00:02:06.137 --> 00:02:09.180
(processor whirs)

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.760
So this mixture has
gotten a little bit flaky,

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.390
so I'm gonna add my vanilla into the milk.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:16.680
Whisk it together

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:19.136
and drizzle it in.

00:02:19.136 --> 00:02:22.137
(processor whirs)

00:02:22.137 --> 00:02:23.460
(processor squeals then stops)

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.520
Okay, well it just decided
to stop on its own.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.080
Sorry.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.250
Didn't mean to bother.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.690
But this looks so good!

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:31.523
By the way,

00:02:31.523 --> 00:02:34.380
this is only one batch for one dough,

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.330
and it's only vanilla.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.450
We actually have to make
a chocolate dough as well.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.770
I have a lot of work to do,

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.630
but we're off to a really good start.

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.030
I wanna shape my dough,
and it's gonna be great.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.350
I hope Jasmine is hungry,

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.540
'cause this is only one Pocky.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:49.473
Oh, man.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.880
The blade chopped off

00:02:53.156 --> 00:02:55.380
a little bit of my spatula.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.210
You know, extra flavor.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.880
I'm using a sieve to dust my flour

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.680
so there are no lumps.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.460
I can't believe that this
is actually just one Pocky.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.590
This...

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.620
It's already so massive!

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:14.490
Shortbread cookies are
very tricky to begin with

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.290
and they're very delicate.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:21.290
So I know that this is a very
sensitive boy right here.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.670
It's wanting to fall apart.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.410
I'm gonna let this sit in the fridge

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:26.730
so it can firm up.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.610
That way, it'll be easier
for me to roll it out.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.230
One vanilla batch down.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.780
I'm going to put this in
the fridge for an hour.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.613
While I wait for that,

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:37.140
I'm gonna make five
more batches of vanilla

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.345
and then I can get
started on my chocolate.

00:03:39.345 --> 00:03:40.710
(jazzy music)

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:43.560
Now all I gotta do are
my chocolate batches.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.390
The process is pretty much the same thing.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.510
The only difference is
I'm adding cocoa powder

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.308
to this batch.

00:03:50.308 --> 00:03:51.330
(processor whirs)

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.280
I don't know if it's
because I have experience

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.480
just making this dough,

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.960
but this is becoming really easy to do.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.930
Okay, adding in my vanilla to my milk.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.840
I think that was the
fastest dough I've made yet.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.070
It's looking good, guys.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:06.090
Looking great.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.290
Growing up in Vietnam,

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:09.060
there wasn't any Pocky,

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.500
but there was something similar.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.870
It's just like shortbread cookie sticks

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.570
and then on the side
there would be sugar dips

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:16.590
or chocolate dips.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.990
I didn't have a proper Pocky stick

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:21.090
until I came over to America,

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.790
and that was life-changing.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:26.070
Alright, this is going in the fridge.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:28.605
I have one more to go and I can move on.

00:04:28.605 --> 00:04:29.790
(upbeat music)

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:34.470
Apparently, Pocky was first sold in 1966.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.716
That's actually not that long ago.

00:04:36.716 --> 00:04:41.716
There are technically
over 50 Pocky flavors.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.550
Here is my chilled batch of vanilla.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.190
This is my chilled batch of chocolate.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:50.010
So after one hour in the fridge,

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.020
it's definitely really firm.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.890
I'm gonna roll this out,
about 30 to 31 inches long

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.530
and then about two inches wide.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.780
I start in the middle right here,

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.870
and just kind of use my fingers

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.460
to spread out the dough.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.650
I just hope that this dough

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.680
doesn't spread too much when it's baking

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.807
because I really need
it to keep its shape.

00:05:13.807 --> 00:05:17.388
(energetic music)

00:05:17.388 --> 00:05:20.337
This looks like a big baguette,

00:05:20.337 --> 00:05:21.630
but it's not.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.930
It's a giant log of cookie.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.850
I'm really scared it's not
going to hold its shape.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:29.550
What I'm gonna do is I'm going to wrap it,

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.680
and keep it wrapped while it's baking

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.930
so it can keep its shape.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.190
For those of you at home

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:38.340
that are worried that
the plastic will melt,

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.650
since this is such a big batch of cookie,

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:41.490
while it's baking,

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:43.290
it's going to create a lot of steam,

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:47.400
and the steam is going to
keep the plastic from melting.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.070
Also, make sure that the ends are tight.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:52.170
It's like a big compound butter.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.370
Really happy about this.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.420
I'm gonna wrap it in aluminum.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.370
I have seven more to go.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.196
Once all of this is rolled out,

00:06:01.196 --> 00:06:05.447
I'm gonna put it into the
oven at 300 for 90 minutes.

00:06:05.447 --> 00:06:06.300
(upbeat music)

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.640
While the giant Pocky sticks are baking,

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.350
I'm gonna work on my toppings.

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:11.880
I have dried strawberries here

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.490
and Oreos that I'm gonna crush up

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:17.010
to make these two flavors,

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.770
because Jasmine wants all of them.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.946
I'm gonna do strawberries first.

00:06:22.946 --> 00:06:25.530
These are freeze-dried strawberries.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:26.836
Run it through a food processor.

00:06:26.836 --> 00:06:28.920
(processor whirs)

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.210
Then I'm gonna run it through a sieve

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:32.370
so there are no chunks in here.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.320
Oh, that looks so good!

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:36.000
These will be for the Pocky sticks,

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.420
and this will be for my snack later.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.450
Now, I'm going to add in my Oreos

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.476
for the cookies and cream.

00:06:44.476 --> 00:06:46.620
(processor whirs)

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:48.090
Super happy with this.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.010
It's actually kind of sticking together

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.810
because of the cream.

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:52.800
Ta-da!

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:53.807
I'm nervous.

00:06:53.807 --> 00:06:54.640
(Tway laughs)

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:58.080
I'm about to work with an
insane amount of chocolate.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.080
It's gonna be tough.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.680
Guys, I was not kidding

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.900
when I said there's going
to be a lot of chocolate,

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.190
because this is a whole lot of chocolate.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.720
I have ruby chocolate,

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.040
semi-sweet chocolate,

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.930
and white chocolate.

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:15.630
The white chocolate is
for the cookies and cream

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:16.800
and matcha flavor.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:18.720
I have to melt all of it,

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:21.754
and I'm gonna start with
the semi-sweet chocolate.

00:07:21.754 --> 00:07:22.860
(grinder clatters)

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.390
Sorry. That was really loud.

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:26.580
I'm trying not to make my water boil

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:28.290
because if my water starts to boil,

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:30.030
it will ruin the chocolate.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.090
So I'm trying to keep it at a simmer.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:36.960
Working with a big giant
spatula is very tiring,

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:38.370
because I can't even hold it

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:39.570
like a regular spatula.

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:43.950
I'm holding it like it's just a big stick.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:48.950
This is actually a cheater
way of tempering chocolate,

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.210
adding coconut oil,

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:53.013
because this is a really
big batch of chocolate

00:07:53.013 --> 00:07:55.740
that I don't want to mess up and waste.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:58.080
So tempering is basically
getting chocolate

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.970
to a right melted temperature,

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:01.230
which is really tricky

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:02.490
because it can bloom

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:03.960
and it can start to seize up

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.730
and you can't use that chocolate anymore.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:06.990
If your temperature's too low,

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:08.790
the chocolate will melt very slow

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:10.830
and it will be a pain in the butt.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.750
The chocolate's looking really good,

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.400
nice and silky.

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:15.960
I hope Jasmine's gonna be happy

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.550
because we're going all out

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:20.190
with all of the chocolate flavors

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:21.273
for her birthday.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:24.000
I have my white chocolate here,

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.020
and the first flavor that
I'm gonna do is matcha.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.760
Whisk all of this together.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:32.490
Mm. I love the smell of matcha.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.610
It's turning out to look
like the actual color

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:38.010
of the matcha Pocky stick,

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.510
and I'm really happy about it.

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:41.970
That's matcha.

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.557
Next up, I have my Oreo crumbles here.

00:08:44.557 --> 00:08:46.530
I'm gonna flavor this chocolate,

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:49.050
and that's for the
cookies and cream Pocky.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:52.110
Just going to add like two pinches

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:53.850
of this crumble in here.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:56.760
Going for that speckled look.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.250
I want it to be kind of like a peek-a-boo,

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.110
not like, "Hey! I'm here!"

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:01.943
You know?

00:09:01.943 --> 00:09:03.570
I gotta work fast here,

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:06.390
'cause I don't want
this chocolate to harden

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:08.817
and ruin all my hard work.

00:09:08.817 --> 00:09:10.080
(jazzy music)

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.070
Hi, my name is Tway,

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.087
and welcome to my chocolate shop.

00:09:13.087 --> 00:09:14.280
(Tway laughs)

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.200
This is a lot of chocolate.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.327
We have our semi-sweet chocolate here,

00:09:19.327 --> 00:09:21.017
ruby chocolate,

00:09:21.017 --> 00:09:22.830
our cookies and cream,

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:24.000
and our matcha.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.240
The only thing missing
are my giant Pocky sticks.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:28.260
So...

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:29.639
Check this out.

00:09:29.639 --> 00:09:30.497
(drum roll)

00:09:30.497 --> 00:09:31.456
Ta-da!

00:09:31.456 --> 00:09:32.790
(crowd cheering sounds)

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:34.950
They held up.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:36.990
I'm so happy about that.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.970
Okay, these are really, really big.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.100
I'm just really happy that they held up

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.780
and they kept the shape,

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:43.980
'cause that was the one thing

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.180
that I was really worried about.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:47.280
These kind of look like baguettes,

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:50.100
but, no, they are big giant cookies.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:52.200
I just don't want it to be ruined.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.510
So I have made an executive decision

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:57.330
to pour it over instead of dipping it in,

00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.090
because I feel like they're
just too fragile to be dipped.

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:01.440
Oh, she feels thick,

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:03.240
but she feels pourable.

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:05.388
So here we go.

00:10:05.388 --> 00:10:06.697
Ooh.

00:10:06.697 --> 00:10:09.405
(Tway gasps)

00:10:09.405 --> 00:10:12.960
(gentle jazz music)

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.060
I love this green color.

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:18.960
Okay, visually, this looks so good.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.000
Next, I'm gonna do the cookies and cream

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:25.410
and it's going right on top
of the chocolate shortbread.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:26.310
They look so good,

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.080
but they have these
little bubbles in there.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:31.353
So I'm gonna gently tap this.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.640
Alright, so let's do a
comparison right now.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:37.500
This is the matcha.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.613
Twins!

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.090
Then this is the cookies and cream.

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:44.070
So I'm looking at the Oreo right now,

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:48.330
and it looks like there's more
of these speckled in there.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:52.260
I'm going to add some
